COOLBOY12 — RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION SCHEMA (structural contract)

ARTIFACT 080 · RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION schema · docs/registry/relationship_type.schema ·
Own: R · RM: R · T: schema · R: CONTRACT · SoT: AUTHORITATIVE · Auth: defining ·
Canon: canonical-about-meaning · CD: yes · Ph/St: P3/3b · Req: RR-16 · BP: §9.4 · RMS: §10.1 ·
H: 079 · S: — · LS: LS-1 · G: — · → 177,277,338,352,375 · Val: definition resolves; versionable;
references only declared entities (063) · Done: schema · Why: LS-3 · Risk: high · ∥: yes

==================================================================================================
0. HOW TO READ THIS FILE
==================================================================================================

NOTATION   This file reuses the local declarative notation of Artifact 067, with the CHECK line
           Artifact 069 added, the REPOSITORY CONVENTION basis label Artifact 071 added, the
           absent word Artifact 073 added, and the dotted parts, list counts and outcomes
           Artifact 077 added. It is an implementation choice, not COOLBOY12 architecture, and
           establishes no repository-wide schema language (SC-080-K). No parser exists for it.

           ELEMENT <name>        a structural element of a materialized Record
           ELEMENT <a>.<b>       part <b> of each value of element <a>; <a>.<b>.<c> is a part of
                                 a part. Structure inside one family element, not a separate
                                 family element
           LAYER                 ENVELOPE (universal, RMS §4) or FAMILY (Registry-model-owned)
           REQUIRED              yes | no — where no, the line says when the carrier is needed
           CARDINALITY           exactly-one | zero-or-one | zero-or-more | one-or-more — how many
                                 times the carrier occurs in the Record. It is never
                                 relationship-type cardinality, which this contract does not
                                 represent (§3 NOT REPRESENTED; OD-079-1)
           CONSTRAINT            what a conforming value must satisfy
           CHECK                   NATIVE      decidable from the Record's own structure and its
                                               expressly declared values
                                   EXTERNAL    needs evidence outside the Record; the line names
                                               the evidence and who supplies it, and this
                                               contract does not claim it established
                                   STATIC      a property of this contract, checked by reading it
                                   REPOSITORY  a property of the change that adds this file
           BASIS                   SOURCE FACT            stated by a governing source
                                   REQUIRED SYNTHESIS     forced by several source facts together
                                   REPOSITORY CONVENTION  a choice of Artifact 067, 069, 071, 073
                                                          or 077, reused
                                   080 CHOICE             a representation decision of this file
                                   SOURCE GAP             not established by any current source
           REJECT                a value that does not conform, with the rule it breaks and its
                                 CHECK

           A part of a part, <a>.<b>.<c>, is this file's one addition to the notation, an 080
           CHOICE: an eligibility entry belongs to one role (§3 role.eligibility). REPOSITORY
           CONVENTION and 080 CHOICE authorize no semantic rule; where a choice is made, the line
           says what it does not decide.

OUTCOMES   A candidate Record has exactly one of the four outcomes of Artifact 077 (REPOSITORY
           CONVENTION), decided in this order; the first that applies is the outcome (§4 X-01):
             REJECT            a rule is shown to be violated: a NATIVE rule fails; an EXTERNAL
                               check establishes a violation; or a status that must be
                               established — the declared status of a named Kind — cannot be
                               established when its owner's check is run: "Undetermined is not
                               permitted." (Artifact 063 RB-6). A known violation is never
                               excused by an unrelated open question.
             UNRESOLVED        no violation is shown, but the Record has a shape whose
                               admissibility the governing sources leave open (§4 S-02, S-03,
                               S-04, D-04, D-05, E-04, E-08). This contract neither accepts nor
                               rejects the shape, and a carrier able to hold it is no authority
                               for it. It is not a success. It is a source gap, not a missing
                               lookup: no check anyone could run today settles it.
             PENDING_EXTERNAL  every NATIVE rule holds and no shape is UNRESOLVED, but one or more
                               EXTERNAL obligations have not been established — because the check
                               has not been run, or, for an obligation other than the declared
                               status of a named Kind, because the check ran and established
                               nothing either way. A pre-final evidence state, not acceptance; an
                               unrun check is never reported as failed.
             CONFORMS          every NATIVE rule holds, every applicable EXTERNAL check has been
                               established by its owner, no shape is UNRESOLVED, and no rule is
                               violated.
           Four evidence states stay apart. Not yet checked: PENDING_EXTERNAL. Checked, and a named
           Kind's required declared status cannot be established: REJECT (RB-6) — never
           PENDING_EXTERNAL and never UNRESOLVED. Checked and shown invalid: REJECT. Answer left
           open by the governing sources themselves: UNRESOLVED. A NATIVE pass alone is never
           CONFORMS. The decision matrix of §4 OUTCOME ORDER applies these states.
           CONFORMS is bounded to this contract. It does not establish that Blueprint §13.3's
           cardinality obligation is met — no carrier for it exists here (OD-079-1); it says
           nothing about what the owning role governs where no Relationship Record is used
           (OD-079-2); and it shows no actual edge's ownership, no resolution by a consumer and no
           version mechanism. The labels are contract vocabulary, never Record fields; no outcome
           named here reports a real Record, and this file implements no validator (§6
           EXECUTION).

STATUS     This contract describes the structure a materialized RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION
           Record must satisfy. It is an authored structural contract under docs/registry/. It is
           not a Registry Record, not canonical data, not a concrete relationship-type
           definition, not a SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record, not a World Relationship Record schema,
           not a relationship-instance schema, not a catalog of relationship types, not a schema
           execution engine and not a universal relationship architecture. Its header copies row
           080's SoT: AUTHORITATIVE, Auth: defining, Canon: canonical-about-meaning and CD: yes
           exactly; those values do not make this file a Record and license no canonical write
           (SC-080-G). Roadmap §0.8 lets this contract be authored before canonical
           materialization: "Structural contracts — rows 067, 069, 071, 073, 077, 080, 082, 084,
           087, 089, 091, 093, 095, 097, 099, 102, 104 — move to docs/registry/<family>.schema".
           Concrete RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION Records are committed only through the Mutation
           Coordinator (row 152) after G-CANON-R. Where this contract differs from the Master
           Blueprint, the Record Model System, the Roadmap, or Artifact 079, those sources are
           right and this contract is wrong.

SPEC       Artifact 079 — docs/registry/relationship_type.md — is the semantic contract this file
           encodes, consumed unchanged (H: 079). This file encodes the structural consequences of
           079 §5–§15 and the handoff of 079 §21, and nothing 079 leaves open: OD-079-1 and
           OD-079-2 stay open (079 §19.1). Artifacts 067, 069, 071, 073 and 077 are precedents for
           notation and representation conventions only: no semantics is taken from the MODEL-,
           KIND-, SUBTYPE-, FIELD- or SCHEMA-DEFINITION families, and none of those rows is a
           dependency of row 080. Artifacts 003, 033, 034, 044, 055, 058, 061, 062, 063, 064 and
           078 are supporting constraints, not entries in H or S.

==================================================================================================
1. RECORD SHAPE
==================================================================================================

RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION RECORD
├── ENVELOPE  partition · kind · object_id · slug · provenance · registry_ref · sot_class
└── FAMILY    definition · role · owning_role · direction
              ├── definition   the governed meaning of the one relationship type
              ├── role         one or more, each:  key · meaning · eligibility
              │                └── eligibility   zero or more, each:  model · kind (zero or one)
              ├── owning_role  exactly one designation of one declared role, by its key
              └── direction    zero or one, with:  from · to — each a declared role, by its key

NOT REPRESENTED   relationship-type cardinality (§3; §6 CARDINALITY; OD-079-1)

Artifact 080 defines exactly these eleven elements: the universal seven-field envelope (RMS §4)
and four family elements. The family elements have seven parts — role.key, role.meaning,
role.eligibility, role.eligibility.model, role.eligibility.kind, direction.from and direction.to.
It defines no other element or part.

That is the inventory of this revision of the contract, not a closure over everything a
RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION Record may later carry. Rows 108–110 keep their authority to
establish Registry-owned evolution, versioning, supersession and deprecation representation, and a
governed revision of this contract may add what they establish (§6 VERSIONABILITY). The envelope,
by contrast, stays exactly seven fields: no later representation becomes an eighth universal field
(RMS §4; P-05).

One type, four carriers. 079 requires that each Record govern one relationship type's meaning,
declare its participant roles and designate exactly one of them as the owning role (079 §5.3; row
079 Done), and attaches direction and per-role eligibility to the type of a relationship in
Blueprint §13.3's sense (079 §9). This contract carries the meaning in definition, the roles in
role, the designation in owning_role and the reading in direction. No carrier alone is the
definition.

Roles are local positions. A role entry declares one position a participant occupies in every
relationship of the type (079 §7). role.key distinguishes it inside this Record and nowhere else:
it is not a Record, a Kind, a subtype, a field or a global code, and it identifies no participant.
owning_role and direction name roles by role.key, so each can be checked against the declared
roles of the same Record (§4).

Three things called "kind" or "type", never merged. The envelope element kind names this Record's
own Kind — always RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION. role.eligibility.kind names a declared Kind whose
Records may stand in a role — for example CHARACTER. The relationship type itself — for example
MEMBER_OF — is neither: it is what this Record defines, and it is not a Kind.

Carrier count is not semantic count. The number of role entries is not relationship-type
cardinality, and a list able to hold three roles does not make a three-role type admissible (§4
S-02, S-03). The number of eligibility entries is not a multiplicity rule. The CARDINALITY lines of
this file count carriers, nothing else.

Not the edges. A Character MEMBER_OF an Organization is an actual relationship, owned by the model
whose mechanism holds it — World's Relationship Record of the member (Blueprint §13.9; I-73). This
contract is the structure of the Registry Record that defines MEMBER_OF. It carries no endpoint,
edge, edge identity, temporal validity, edge provenance, history or back-reference (079 RT-079-16;
P-04).

==================================================================================================
2. ENVELOPE — the universal seven (RMS §4; Artifact 033)
==================================================================================================

Types, defaults, nullability and serialization of the envelope fields are not established by the
governing sources (Artifact 033) and are not stated here.

ELEMENT     partition
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  R — the Registry partition
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION is a Registry Kind (RMS §10.1); 079 §5.2,
            RT-079-01
REJECT      W, E, P, V or I — for example a World Record, such as a Relationship Record, is never
            a RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION                          (RT-079-01)      NATIVE

ELEMENT     kind
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  identifies the declared Registry Kind RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION (Kind 6 of RMS
            §10.1) — this Record's own Kind, never the Kind of any participant
            (role.eligibility.kind) and never the relationship type it defines. The constraint is
            symbolic. No two-character Registry Kind code is established; none is minted here
            (SC-080-I). Blueprint §13.6's RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEF is a source alias, not another
            Kind (064 §5; SC-080-A).
CHECK       NATIVE against the symbolic Kind; against a code only once the Registry's codes are
            bound by their own row (row 117)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §10.1; Artifact 064 §6, §13; 079 RT-079-01
REJECT      KIND-DEFINITION, SCHEMA-DEFINITION or any other Registry Kind            NATIVE
            a participant's Kind (for example CHARACTER) placed here                NATIVE
            a relationship type's name (for example MEMBER_OF) placed here           NATIVE
            an invented code presented as established                               NATIVE

ELEMENT     object_id
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the object identity component under the universal identity grammar
            [PARTITION]-[KIND]-[OBJECT_ID]-[SLUG]. It is this definition Record's own identity —
            not the relationship type's name, not a role key, not a participant's identifier, not
            an edge's identity and not a Relationship Record's identity (079 RS-079-2, RS-079-3).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value
            STATIC — this contract makes no family element a substitute for it
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4, §5; Artifact 034; 079 RS-079-1 to RS-079-3

ELEMENT     slug
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  decoration only; never identity, never a lookup key, never the basis of resolution or
            ownership
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value
            STATIC — this contract gives slug no identity, lookup, resolution or ownership role
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §5; Artifact 033; 079 RS-079-2

ELEMENT     provenance
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it: this definition Record's own provenance
            capture. Provenance meaning is not defined here. The provenance of an actual
            relationship — "provenanced" in §13.3 — belongs to each relationship and the model
            that holds it (079 §6), and is never carried here, in this element or another.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4 (provenance capture universal, meaning model-owned); Artifact 033;
            079 §6, RT-079-16
REJECT      absent — a definition Record's provenance is not optional        (RMS §4)  NATIVE
            replaced by an edge's provenance                                (RT-079-16) EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     registry_ref
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the universal envelope field, unchanged. This contract attaches no referent,
            self-reference convention, bootstrap target or resolution meaning to it, and it
            carries neither a participant Kind nor an owning role (SC-080-R).
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033 leaves its referent unresolved; Blueprint §9.4:
            "Reference resolution is not Registry work"

ELEMENT     sot_class
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it: a Record-level source-of-truth class, which
            Artifact 033 §5.7 identifies as one of the Blueprint's five — AUTHORITATIVE · DERIVED
            · CACHED · TEMPORARY · EXTERNAL. No value is fixed here. Row 080's manifest SoT and
            Canon are not Record-level values and are not copied into it, and sot_class is not
            canonicality (I-104).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; membership of the five Record-level classes
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4 ("Source-of-truth classification | §29.6a — five classes");
            Artifact 033 §5.7; Artifact 016
REJECT      DEV-ENV — a repository-artifact class, "not a record-level value" (Artifact 033 §5.7)
                                                                                     NATIVE
            canonical-about-meaning, or any Canon value, written as a source-of-truth class
                                                                        (I-104)      NATIVE

==================================================================================================
3. FAMILY — RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION content (Registry-model-owned; not envelope fields)
==================================================================================================

definition, role and owning_role are required in every Record. direction and role.eligibility are
present or absent as §4 S-04 requires. No family element or part has a default value. A required
element or part may not be left empty, and an absent part is absent — not an empty value, a null
placeholder or a wildcard (REPOSITORY CONVENTION, 073). Types and serialization of the family
elements are not established by the governing sources and are not stated here; this contract fixes
structure, not an encoding.

ELEMENT     definition
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the governed account of one relationship type's meaning: what a relationship of this
            type says (079 §5.3 item 1; 064 §13 Q4). A Registry definition "Governs; never
            instantiates" (RMS §6.1). Non-empty. Its internal form is not prescribed.
            A name. The content may state the name by which the type is known — for example
            MEMBER_OF. A name is not this Record's identity, is not unique by this contract, and is
            no lookup or resolution key (079 RS-079-2). No name element is defined (§6
            REPRESENTATION).
            What it carries none of (§4 M-01 to M-05): a second, independently governed type or a
            catalog of types; any actual endpoint, participant identifier, edge, edge identity,
            temporal validity, edge provenance, history or graph data; a statement contradicting
            role, owning_role, direction or eligibility; a cardinality presented as the type's
            governed cardinality while OD-079-1 is open; an application of the owning role that
            the governing model's architecture does not establish (OD-079-2); executable
            behaviour; a domain instance, domain state or runtime object as authority; a
            reference in a relation this family does not establish. Unstructured prose is no
            exemption from the reference boundary (§6 REFERENCES).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, non-empty.
            EXTERNAL — the content limits are semantic and not decidable from structure; they are
            judged against 079, and this contract does not claim them proven. A non-empty value
            is not thereby an adequate meaning.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 §5.2, §5.3, RT-079-02, RT-079-16, RT-079-22, RF-079-2 to
            RF-079-5; RMS §6.1; 064 §13 Q1, Q4. The single carrier, the element NAME and the
            non-empty rule follow Artifacts 067, 069, 071, 073 and 077 (REPOSITORY CONVENTION).
            Carrying a type's name only as content is an 080 CHOICE.
REJECT      no value, or an empty one                                (079 §5.3)        NATIVE
            content defining two independently governed types         (RT-079-02; M-01) EXTERNAL
            content shown to be a statement of edges, for example "Character A is a member of
            Organization B" as the type's content                    (RT-079-16; M-01) EXTERNAL
            content using W-CH-000001-Maximus as what "the member" means
                                                                     (RF-079-2; M-05)  EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     role
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY one-or-more — each value is one declared participant role, with the parts role.key,
            role.meaning and role.eligibility
CONSTRAINT  each value declares one participant role of this type: a position a participant
            occupies in every relationship of the type (079 §7). The roles are declared here, not
            inferred from the type's name, a participant Kind, a domain instance, entry order,
            direction or an example (079 §7, RT-079-03).
            At least one: a Record with no declared role has no role for owning_role to designate
            (RT-079-05). This element fixes no further count. How many roles a type may declare
            is the arity rule of §4 S-02 and S-03. For World, the sources fix two endpoints per
            edge (Blueprint §13.9: "An edge joins two objects.") and show two distinct roles;
            they do not fix that every endpoint occupies its own declared role, so one or more
            than two World roles is UNRESOLVED, not rejected (S-02). For other models, the count
            is what their own architecture establishes (S-03). A count of role entries is never
            read as a count of endpoints.
            Unordered. The order in which entries are written carries no meaning, and no rule of
            this contract reads it (079 §8.2 item 4; RT-079-08).
            A role is part of this one definition. It is not a Record, a Kind, a subtype, a field,
            a participant or a participant's identifier, and has no identity outside this Record
            (079 §7).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; at least one entry; each entry's parts; key uniqueness (§4 R-03)
            EXTERNAL — the count against the governing model's arity (§4 S-02, S-03)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — the type carries "its participant roles" (Blueprint §13.3); the Registry
            holds "relationship-type definitions with their participant roles" (§9.4); row 079
            Done. REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — distinguishable and declared (079 §7; RT-079-03). 080
            CHOICE — a list of role entries; unordered; the element NAME. 079 §7: "How roles are
            named or identified is 080's."
REJECT      no entry                                                  (R-01)           NATIVE

ELEMENT     role.key
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each role
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  a local designator that distinguishes this role from every other role of the same
            Record, and by which owning_role and direction name it.
            Form. Non-empty, with no leading or trailing whitespace, and not shaped as a Record
            identifier under the universal grammar.
            Matching. Exact, character for character, with no case folding, trimming or other
            normalization. A designation names a role only if it equals that role's key exactly.
            Uniqueness. No two keys of one Record are equal, and no two are equal ignoring letter
            case: member and Member cannot both be keys, so no designation can be read two ways.
            Local only. A key means nothing outside this Record. It is not a Registry Kind, a kind
            code, a role Record, a global role code or a member of a universal role vocabulary.
            Spellings such as source, target, subject or object receive no meaning from this
            contract, and a key's spelling is never a basis for ownership or direction (079 §7
            "No universal role grammar"). The key does not state the role's meaning — role.meaning
            does — and identifies no participant.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; non-empty; no leading or trailing whitespace; not
            shaped as a Record identifier; uniqueness, exact and ignoring case
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — each declared role is distinguishable within the type, because
            the owning role must designate exactly one of them (079 §7; RT-079-03 to RT-079-05).
            080 CHOICE — a keyed form, exact matching, case-insensitive uniqueness, the
            whitespace rule and the part NAME (§6 REPRESENTATION). The choice decides no role
            vocabulary and no key spelling.
REJECT      absent, or empty                                          (R-02)           NATIVE
            two keys equal, or equal ignoring case — member and Member  (R-03)           NATIVE
            a key with leading or trailing whitespace                 (R-04)           NATIVE
            a key shaped as a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-<slug>    (R-04)           NATIVE

ELEMENT     role.meaning
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each role
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  what occupying this role means in a relationship of the type — for MEMBER_OF, the
            member, and the organization the member belongs to (079 §7). Non-empty. Stated by
            this definition, never taken from an actual participant, a Kind, an instance or an
            example (079 §7 "Held by the definition"; RF-079-2). It states the position, not who
            may stand in it (role.eligibility), not ownership (owning_role) and not the reading
            (direction).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, non-empty
            EXTERNAL — adequacy is semantic and judged against 079; this contract does not claim
            it proven
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — "A role's meaning is stated in the definition" and "Its meaning is
            part of the type's meaning" (079 §7). 080 CHOICE — a per-role carrier rather than
            leaving each role's meaning to definition alone, so that every declared role has a
            stated meaning; the part NAME.
REJECT      absent, or empty                                          (R-02)           NATIVE
            meaning taken from a domain instance, e.g. "whatever W-CH-000001-Maximus is"
                                                                     (RF-079-2)        EXTERNAL
            a participant identifier given as the meaning            (079 §7)          EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     role.eligibility
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each role
REQUIRED    no — at least one entry on each of the two roles of a two-role World type, as this
            contract's representation of §13.3's legality obligation (§4 S-04); otherwise as
            S-04 states
CARDINALITY zero-or-more — each value is one eligibility entry, with the parts
            role.eligibility.model and role.eligibility.kind
CONSTRAINT  each entry states one category of participant that may stand in this role: the
            type's "legality constraints (which kinds may stand at each end)" (Blueprint §13.3),
            stated per role (079 §9.4). Several entries list several Kinds, each of which may
            stand in the role. No combination, exclusion, negation, condition, precedence or
            count rule among entries is represented, and the number of entries is no multiplicity
            rule (SC-080-N).
            Absence. A role with no entry states no eligibility. That is not "every Kind may
            stand" and not "no Kind may stand"; its effect is §4 S-04. It is also not an
            undeclared Kind: absence fails, where it fails, under S-04, and no Kind is checked
            for it under E-07. An explicitly empty value, a null placeholder and a wildcard are
            not absence and do not conform (§4 E-03, E-06). "All Kinds" has no representation
            (SC-080-N).
            Declaration level. An entry names a declared Record Model and, normally, a declared
            Kind of that model, by declaration reference: the declared Model and Kind themselves,
            not a MODEL-DEFINITION or KIND-DEFINITION Record (079 RF-079-1; Artifact 063 §8.2,
            §8.3). Naming them creates, declares or admits nothing (Artifact 057 §9; RT-079-15),
            and overrides neither Artifact 058 nor the model's own constraints (§4 E-09).
CHECK       NATIVE — each entry well formed (below); no two identical entries in one role
            EXTERNAL — whether entries are required (§4 S-04), and the checks of the parts
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — Blueprint §13.3; RMS §10.3 (declared Record Models and declared Kinds
            are admissible). REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 §9.4, RF-079-1, RT-079-15. An entry as a
            model with an optional Kind follows 069's subject_model and subject_kind, 073's
            domain_model and domain_kind and 077's applicability (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). A
            per-role list, the duplicate rule, the declaration-reference form and the part NAME
            are 080 CHOICES (§6 REPRESENTATION).
REJECT      two identical entries in one role                         (E-05)           NATIVE
            an explicitly empty, null or placeholder value            (E-06)           NATIVE

ELEMENT     role.eligibility.model
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each eligibility entry
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   W | E | P | R | V | I
              W  World       E  Epistemic   P  Production
              R  Registry    V  Visual      I  Issue
            The declared Record Model whose own Kind taxonomy declares role.eligibility.kind, or,
            in an entry without a Kind, the model named as the category — an UNRESOLVED shape (§4
            E-04). It names the declared Record Model itself — the six constitutionally
            established models are the declared models Artifact 063 admits (§7 row 2). It is a
            declaration reference, not a MODEL-DEFINITION reference, and confers no ownership.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; membership of the closed set. Membership is the
            declared-status check for a model: the closed set is the set of declared Record Models
            (RMS §2; Artifact 063 §7 row 2).
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §2; RMS §10.3; Artifact 063 §7 row 2. The closed set follows 069,
            073 and 077 (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). Writing the model in every entry, Kind-scoped ones
            included, is an 080 CHOICE: it tells the EXTERNAL check of role.eligibility.kind whose
            taxonomy to consult. It decides neither whether Model-only eligibility is admissible
            nor whether one type may have participants of different models (SC-080-N).
REJECT      absent — including an entry naming a Kind and no model    (E-01)           NATIVE
            two or more values in one entry                           (E-01)           NATIVE
            a value outside the set, e.g. S "Simulation" claimed as a seventh model
                                                                     (E-02; RMS §2)    NATIVE
            a Record identifier, or a MODEL-DEFINITION Record's identifier R-<kind>-…
                                                                     (E-01; RF-079-1)  NATIVE

ELEMENT     role.eligibility.kind
LAYER       FAMILY — part of each eligibility entry
REQUIRED    no — present in a Kind-scoped entry; absent in a Model-only entry, which is
            UNRESOLVED (§4 E-04)
CARDINALITY zero-or-one
CONSTRAINT  names one Kind exactly as the Kind taxonomy of role.eligibility.model declares it —
            for example CHARACTER under W. The name is read only within role.eligibility.model.
            It names the Kind itself: never a Record of that Kind (RF-079-2), never the Kind's
            KIND-DEFINITION Record (RF-079-1; Artifact 063 §8.3), never a two-character kind code
            (SC-080-I), never a subtype, never a runtime object (RF-079-4), never a wildcard.
            Declared status. The named Kind must be a declared Kind of role.eligibility.model,
            with that status established by the owning model's own Kind architecture (RF-079-1;
            Artifact 063 §7 row 3, §8.3). Naming it does not admit it (Artifact 057 §9).
            Form. A declaration reference to the declared Kind, not an R → R reference to its
            KIND-DEFINITION Record. Naming a declared Kind does not, by itself, establish a
            semantic dependency (Artifact 062 D-9; RF-079-7, RF-079-8).
CHECK       NATIVE — at most one value; the value is not shaped as a Record identifier under the
            universal grammar; the pair (role.eligibility.model, role.eligibility.kind) is not
            (W, WSV); the value is not the wildcard *.
            EXTERNAL — declared status, and that the Kind is role.eligibility.model's. The proof
            comes from the owning model's Kind architecture (Artifact 063 SC-063-H; SC-080-L).
            This contract does not define or prove that evidence. Downstream legality validation
            may enforce it under its own contract; row 112 independently enforces its narrower
            domain-instance reference prohibition. An undetermined Kind is not legal (Artifact 063
            RB-6).
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 §9.4, RF-079-1, RF-079-2, RF-079-7; Artifact 063 §6, §8.3,
            SC-063-G (the form of a declaration reference is the family's to fix). The declaration
            form and naming the Kind by its declared name follow 069, 073 and 077 (REPOSITORY
            CONVENTION). Making the part optional, so that a Model-only entry can be written and
            marked UNRESOLVED rather than made unwritable, is an 080 CHOICE. (W, WSV): "WSV is
            World state, not a Kind" (row 231); "the WSV singleton is not a Kind" (Roadmap PART
            III, LS-1).
REJECT      two or more Kinds in one entry                            (E-01)           NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-<slug> — a domain instance (E-03; RF-079-2) NATIVE
            a KIND-DEFINITION Record's identifier, R-<kind>-…          (E-03; RF-079-1) NATIVE
            WSV under W                                               (E-03; row 231)  NATIVE
            the wildcard *                                            (E-03)           NATIVE
            a name role.eligibility.model has not declared — a candidate, a rejected candidate,
            a subtype such as GENERATED-IMAGE under V, or a word meant as "any Kind"
                                                                     (E-07; RF-079-1)  EXTERNAL
            a declared name under the wrong model, e.g. CHARACTER under P
                                                                     (E-07)            EXTERNAL
            a kind code, e.g. CH, written in place of the Kind's name  (SC-080-I)      EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     owning_role
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the one owning-role designation: the role.key of exactly one role declared in this
            Record — the participant role that owns the edge (Blueprint §13.9; 079 §8.2).
            One carrier. The designation is made once, here. No role entry carries an owner flag,
            and no second element repeats or qualifies the designation, so no two carriers can
            disagree (§4 O-03).
            Stated, never defaulted. Nothing substitutes for it: not entry order, not the only
            role of a one-role Record, not direction, not a key's spelling or a role's meaning, not
            a participant Kind, not creation order or editing context (079 §8.2 item 4;
            RT-079-08; §13.9: the rule "requires no tie-breaking").
            A role, not a thing. It names a role of this definition — never a Record, a
            participant, a model, the Registry partition, a storage location or a Relationship
            Record (079 §8.2 item 5).
            Validity, not application. Every Record of the family carries it, whether or not the
            model that uses the type holds Relationship Records (079 §8.5 A; RT-079-25). It states
            which role owns. What that does to actual connections is not represented here: where
            Relationship Records are used, the endpoint occupying the role holds the edge (I-73;
            §13.9), which rows 197–199 and 224 implement; elsewhere it is open (OD-079-2). A
            structural pass of this element proves nothing about any actual edge.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; equal, exactly, to the role.key of exactly one role
            of this Record
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — "The relationship type definition in the Registry declares which
            participant role owns the edge." (Blueprint §13.9); "Exactly one endpoint owns it"
            (§13.9); row 079 Done; Roadmap PART III LS-3 ("including the owning-role
            declaration"). REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — exactly one, one of the type's own roles (079 §8.2
            items 1–3; RT-079-04, RT-079-05). 080 CHOICE — a single designation by role.key rather
            than per-role flags; the element NAME.
REJECT      absent                                                    (O-01)           NATIVE
            two or more values, or an owner flag on a role beside or instead of it
                                                                     (O-03)           NATIVE
            a value equal to no role.key — e.g. observer when the roles are member and
            organization                                              (O-04)           NATIVE
            a value equal to a key only ignoring case — MEMBER for the key member  (O-04) NATIVE
            a value matching two roles — possible only where R-03 fails  (O-05)        NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-<slug>                   (O-04; 079 §8.2) NATIVE

ELEMENT     direction
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    no — required on a two-role World type, as this contract's representation of
            §13.3's direction obligation (§4 S-04); otherwise as S-04 states
CARDINALITY zero-or-one — with the parts direction.from and direction.to
CONSTRAINT  how a relationship of the type reads from one declared role to another (079 §9.2):
            MEMBER_OF reads from the member to the organization.
            Its own declaration. Direction neither derives from owning_role nor determines it.
            direction.from may be the owning role or another role; both conform (§4 D-03). In
            each of §13.9's four examples the owning role happens to be the role the type's name
            reads from; no source makes that a rule (079 §9.2).
            No default. Absence is not a direction, and nothing derives one from entry order,
            keys or names.
            Not represented: an inverse type, a reversal rule, symmetry, transitivity, reflexivity,
            a direction vocabulary or token set, or a reading that is the same from both ends
            (SC-080-N; 079 SC-079-F, SC-079-Q).
CHECK       NATIVE — at most one; when present, both parts present
            EXTERNAL — whether it is required (§4 S-04)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — the type carries "its direction" (Blueprint §13.3), and every relationship
            is "typed, directional" (§13.3). REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 §9.2, RT-079-13. 080 CHOICE —
            an ordered pair of declared roles; optional, with its presence governed by §4 S-04;
            the element NAME. The sources oblige a §13.3 type to carry its direction; they do
            not name this element. The choice is not offered as the only representation a
            governing source could establish (§6 REPRESENTATION).
REJECT      present with a part missing                               (D-01)           NATIVE

ELEMENT     direction.from
ELEMENT     direction.to
LAYER       FAMILY — parts of direction
REQUIRED    yes, when direction is present
CARDINALITY exactly-one each
CONSTRAINT  direction.from names the role the type reads from, direction.to the role it reads
            to, each by the exact role.key of a role declared in this Record. Local referential
            integrity: a part that names no declared role does not conform. from and to naming the
            same role is UNRESOLVED (§4 D-04), not a statement of symmetry.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value each; each equal, exactly, to one role.key
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 §9.2 ("reads from one role to another"). 080 CHOICE — the
            parts, their NAMES and naming roles by role.key.
REJECT      a part naming no declared role                            (D-02)           NATIVE
            a part with two values                                    (D-01)           NATIVE
            a part holding a Record identifier or a Kind name rather than a role key
                                                                     (D-02)           NATIVE

NOT REPRESENTED   relationship-type cardinality

            Source fact. The Registry-defined type of a relationship in §13.3's sense carries
            "its cardinality" (Blueprint §13.3); cardinality is governed type content (079 §9.3).
            Source gap. No source states what it bounds — per role, per participant, per
            relationship or otherwise — its value set, a default, a notation, or whether its
            meaning is uniform across models (OD-079-1; 079 §9.3).
            Treatment. This revision takes the omission route 079 §9.3 permits while OD-079-1 is
            open — "leave cardinality unrepresented, recording that the omission defers §13.3 and
            does not deny it". No element, part, value or token carries relationship-type
            cardinality, and none is reserved.
            What the omission does and does not do:
              — it defers the requirement; it does not deny that cardinality is a type concern;
              — it neither satisfies nor closes OD-079-1;
              — it authorizes no downstream enforcement of a cardinality on edges, and no type set
                may present a cardinality as checkable under this contract;
              — it does not prevent a governed representation once an authoritative source closes
                OD-079-1: a later governed revision of this contract may add one;
              — a CONFORMS outcome never reports §13.3's cardinality obligation as met (§0).
            Not cardinality. The CARDINALITY lines of this file count carriers. The number of role
            entries is arity, governed by §4 S-02 and S-03. Artifact 077's occurrence.cardinality
            is field-occurrence cardinality in a SCHEMA-DEFINITION, and Artifact 078's
            "cardinality/required" is schema-side field composition; neither is relationship-type
            cardinality, and neither resolves OD-079-1 (079 §9.3).
CHECK       NATIVE — no cardinality element or part (P-01A)
            EXTERNAL — no cardinality presented as governed type content in definition (§4 M-03)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — Blueprint §13.3. SOURCE GAP — OD-079-1 (079 §19.1). The omission is the
            route 079 §9.3 names; choosing it for this revision is an 080 CHOICE.
REJECT      a cardinality, multiplicity, minimum or maximum element or part, per role or per type
                                                                     (P-01A)          NATIVE
            a one-to-one, one-to-many or many-to-many token, an L..U bound, or a default such as
            zero, one or unlimited, carried anywhere in the family structure   (P-01A)  NATIVE
            a placeholder or deferred-value token standing for cardinality    (P-01A)  NATIVE
            definition content presenting a cardinality as the type's governed cardinality
                                                                     (M-03)           EXTERNAL

==================================================================================================
4. CROSS-ELEMENT RULES
==================================================================================================

ROLE INTEGRITY

R-01  no role entry                                                     → REJECT     NATIVE
R-02  a role entry without role.key or role.meaning, with an empty one, or with two values of
      either                                                            → REJECT     NATIVE
R-03  two role.key values equal, or equal ignoring letter case          → REJECT     NATIVE
R-04  a role.key with leading or trailing whitespace, or shaped as a Record identifier
                                                                        → REJECT     NATIVE

BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — roles declared and distinguishable (079 §7; RT-079-03). 080
            CHOICE — R-03's case rule and R-04.

OWNING ROLE — the five cases

  owning_role                                     result
  case 1   absent                                 REJECT     O-01                       NATIVE
  case 2   one value, equal to exactly one key    satisfies the owning-role declaration
                                                  requirement; every other rule still applies
                                                  O-02                       NATIVE
  case 3   two or more values, or a second
           designating carrier                    REJECT     O-03                       NATIVE
  case 4   one value, equal to no key             REJECT     O-04                       NATIVE
  case 5   one value, equal to more than one key  REJECT     O-05                       NATIVE

O-01  no owning_role                                                    → REJECT     NATIVE
O-02  exactly one owning_role, equal to the role.key of exactly one declared role — the only
      shape that satisfies the owning-role declaration requirement (079 §8.2; row 079 Done)
O-03  two or more owning_role values; an owner flag, marker or ordering convention on a role; or
      any second element designating an owner                           → REJECT     NATIVE
O-04  an owning_role equal to no role.key — including one equal only ignoring case
                                                                        → REJECT     NATIVE
O-05  an owning_role equal to more than one role.key. Only possible where R-03 already fails;
      stated so that ambiguity is never read as a choice              → REJECT     NATIVE
O-06  nothing substitutes for O-02: a Record whose owner could be guessed — from the first entry,
      from the only role, from direction.from, from a key spelled owner or source, from a
      role.meaning — and that has no owning_role is O-01                → REJECT     NATIVE

BASIS       SOURCE FACT — Blueprint §13.9; row 079 Done; Roadmap PART III LS-3. REQUIRED SYNTHESIS
            — 079 §8.2 items 1–4, RT-079-04 to RT-079-06, RT-079-08. 080 CHOICE — the single
            carrier that makes case 3 a NATIVE check. The five cases are the obligation of 079
            §8.2 written out for this representation.

What O-02 proves and does not prove. It proves that the definition declares exactly one of its own
roles as owning role — definition validity (079 §8.5 A). It proves nothing about an actual edge:
that an edge has one authoritative owner is instance behaviour, checked where Relationship Records
are used (§13.9: "blocked by the linter"; rows 197–199, 224), and what the declaration governs
where they are not used is open (OD-079-2). No rule of this contract makes a Record UNRESOLVED or
REJECT because OD-079-2 is open.

DIRECTION

D-01  direction present without both parts, or with two values for a part
                                                                        → REJECT     NATIVE
D-02  direction.from or direction.to equal to no role.key               → REJECT     NATIVE
D-03  no rule relates direction.from to owning_role. Equal or different, both conform under D;
      neither is inferred from the other                                (STATIC)
D-04  direction.from equal to direction.to — a reading from a role to itself. No symmetry
      meaning is given to it (SC-079-Q; SC-079-F)                       → UNRESOLVED
D-05  direction present on a Record with more than two roles — whether one from/to pair states
      such a type's direction is not established (SC-079-E; SC-079-F)   → UNRESOLVED

BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 §9.2, RT-079-13. 080 CHOICE — D-01, D-02. SOURCE GAP — D-04,
            D-05.

ELIGIBILITY

E-01  an eligibility entry without role.eligibility.model, or with two values of either part
                                                                        → REJECT     NATIVE
E-02  role.eligibility.model outside W | E | P | R | V | I              → REJECT     NATIVE
E-03  role.eligibility.kind shaped as a Record identifier, the pair (W, WSV), or the wildcard *
                                                                        → REJECT     NATIVE
E-04  an entry with role.eligibility.model and no role.eligibility.kind — Model-only
      eligibility (SC-079-G)                                            → UNRESOLVED
E-05  two identical entries in one role                                 → REJECT     NATIVE
E-06  an explicitly empty, null or placeholder eligibility value        → REJECT     NATIVE
E-07  role.eligibility.kind not a declared Kind of role.eligibility.model, or its declared status
      cannot be established when checked (Artifact 063 RB-6)            → REJECT     EXTERNAL
E-08  the eligibility entries of the Record, across all roles, name more than one Record Model —
      participants of different models (SC-079-G; Artifact 058 §8.4)   → UNRESOLVED
E-09  eligibility contrary to a rule Artifact 058 states, or to a named model's own constraint —
      for example World's: "no World field may reference an issue, tier, medium, artifact, or
      the real world" (RMS §7)                                          → REJECT     EXTERNAL

BASIS       SOURCE FACT — Blueprint §13.3; RMS §2, §10.3; Artifact 063 RB-6. REQUIRED SYNTHESIS —
            079 §9.4, RF-079-1, RT-079-15. 080 CHOICE — E-01, E-05, E-06 and the * token of E-03.
            SOURCE GAP — E-04, E-08.

E-07 and E-08 are different rules on purpose. E-07 is Artifact 063's fail-closed rule for the
declared status of a named Kind: an undetermined Kind is not legal. E-08 is a cross-model question
Artifact 058 neither grants nor forbids where no source states the edge (058 §8.4); spelling two
model codes establishes no permission, and this contract does not turn 063's category rule into a
cross-model permission matrix. A Record under E-08 is still checked by E-07 and E-09 for every Kind
it names, and a violation found there makes it REJECT (X-01).

SCOPE AND ARITY — evidence about the governing model

S-01  Which Record Model's relationship architecture governs the type, and whether the type is of
      a relationship in Blueprint §13.3's sense, are EXTERNAL evidence. Their owner is the type
      set in which the definition is authored and that model's relationship architecture: rows
      198 with 197 for W; 277 with 276 for E; 338 for P; 356 for V; 366 for I. This contract
      carries no model-scope element (§6 REPRESENTATION): a carrier would restate, not supply,
      that evidence.                                                                  EXTERNAL
S-02  World role count. What the sources establish, and what they do not:
        established — an actual World edge joins two endpoints (Blueprint §13.9: "An edge joins
        two objects."), and the type states legality "at each end" (§13.3);
        shown — two distinct roles, in §13.9's four examples and 079 §17 Examples A–D. With two
        distinct roles the endpoints divide them: exactly one endpoint occupies the owning role
        (079 §8.4), and the other endpoint, which as a participant occupies a role (079 §7),
        occupies the other — one role at each end;
        not established — that each endpoint occupies its own declared role, or that no
        endpoint occupies two. 079 leaves open how World types a relationship whose two
        endpoints stand in the same role (SC-079-Q), and no source maps declared roles onto
        endpoints one-to-one (SC-080-T).
      The count of role entries is therefore not read as a count of endpoints:
        two role entries — the shape the sources show; every other rule still applies
        one role entry — both endpoints would occupy the one role, which is then the owning
        role, while 079 §8.4 requires exactly one endpoint in it; how World types such a
        relationship is World's (SC-079-Q)                             → UNRESOLVED
        three or more role entries — two endpoints cannot occupy three roles one each, and no
        source establishes or excludes an endpoint occupying more than one (SC-080-T)
                                                                        → UNRESOLVED
      Neither open shape is accepted, and neither is rejected on the endpoint count alone. The
      World count applies only once S-01 establishes that the type is World's.
S-03  A type of any other model has the role count its model's relationship architecture
      establishes.
        a count that architecture contradicts                          → REJECT     EXTERNAL
        no count established by that architecture (SC-079-E)            → UNRESOLVED
      No count — two included — is assumed for these models (079 §7; PI-23 of 079). No Registry
      relationship type set exists (079 §8.5, R row), so a type claimed for R falls in the second
      case.
S-04  Direction and per-role eligibility. The source obligation: "Every relationship has a
      Registry-defined type carrying its participant roles, its direction, its cardinality,
      and its legality constraints (which kinds may stand at each end)." — one of what Blueprint
      §13.3 lists as "unchanged and constitutional". This contract represents the direction
      obligation by direction and the legality obligation by role.eligibility (§3), and does not
      represent cardinality (OD-079-1). The presence requirements below are those
      representations; the sources name neither carrier.
        two-role World type — scope established, because World types are in §13.3's scope:
        §13.3 describes the reified relationship whose packaging is World's (§13.3 scoping
        note; RMS §15 World row "reified"; 079 §9.1, §9.5):
          direction absent — the type carries no direction in the only form this contract
          defines; the form, a reading from one role to the other, is the one 079 §9.2
          establishes                                                  → REJECT     EXTERNAL
          a role with no eligibility entry — the type carries no legality constraint for that
          end in the only form this contract defines                   → REJECT     EXTERNAL
          Why every role: §13.3 states legality "at each end", 079 §9.4 states it per role, and
          in the two-role shape each role is at one end (S-02). Why at least one entry: that is
          this contract's representation — an absent list states nothing (§3 role.eligibility),
          and a constraint admitting every Kind, or no Kind, has no representation here
          (SC-080-N).
          This REJECT is not an undeclared-Kind finding; no Kind is checked for it (E-07).
        one-role or three-or-more-role World type, UNRESOLVED under S-02 — how §13.3's direction
        and per-end legality are carried is part of the open shape. S-04 adds no REJECT for an
        absent carrier; anything present is still checked by D and E
        scope established not to apply by the governing architecture: no presence requirement
        from §13.3; anything present is still checked by D and E
        scope neither established nor excluded — the case 079 SC-079-H records for E, P, V and
        I until their rows answer it, whether or not direction and eligibility are present
                                                                        → UNRESOLVED
      Evidence order. Both REJECTs need S-01's evidence that the type is World's. Until it is
      established, an absent carrier is PENDING_EXTERNAL on S-04, not REJECT: absence is no
      violation until the scope that requires the carrier is shown.
S-05  The owning role's application is not a scope question of this contract. A Record of E, P,
      V or I is never UNRESOLVED, PENDING_EXTERNAL or REJECT because OD-079-2 is open: the
      declaration is definition validity, and its application is not represented (079 §8.5).

BASIS       SOURCE FACT — Blueprint §13.3, §13.9; I-73; RMS §15. REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 §7, §8.4,
            §8.5, §9.1, §9.5; that World types fall in §13.3's scope, and that two distinct roles
            sit one at each end (S-02, S-04). SOURCE GAP — S-02's one-role case (SC-079-Q) and
            three-or-more case (SC-080-T), S-03 (SC-079-E), S-04's open scope (SC-079-H). 080
            CHOICE — S-01's evidence route instead of a model-scope element; S-04's carriers and
            its at-least-one-entry form.

DEFINITION CONTENT

M-01  content defining more than one independently governed type, or stating actual edges,
      endpoints, participant identifiers, edge identity, validity, provenance or history as the
      type's content                                                    → REJECT     EXTERNAL
M-02  content contradicting role, owning_role, direction or eligibility — e.g. naming a different
      owning role                                                       → REJECT     EXTERNAL
M-03  content presenting a cardinality — a bound, a value set, a default, a one-to-one or
      one-to-many classification — as the type's governed cardinality while OD-079-1 is open
                                                                        → REJECT     EXTERNAL
M-04  content stating what the owning role governs inside a mechanism with no Relationship
      Record, where the governing model's architecture establishes no such thing (OD-079-2)
                                                                        → REJECT     EXTERNAL
M-05  content using a domain instance, domain state or runtime object as authority, carrying
      executable behaviour, or carrying a reference in a relation this family does not establish
      (RF-079-2 to RF-079-5)                                            → REJECT     EXTERNAL

BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 079 RT-079-02, RT-079-16, RT-079-22, §8.5, §9.3, RF-079-2 to
            RF-079-5. M-02 follows 077's O-09 (REPOSITORY CONVENTION). M-03 and M-04 keep 079's
            two open decisions from being closed inside content.

OUTCOME ORDER

X-01  Outcomes follow §0: a REJECT anywhere in the Record outranks every UNRESOLVED shape, and an
      UNRESOLVED shape outranks PENDING_EXTERNAL. No shape, admissible or not, makes a Record
      CONFORMS while an EXTERNAL check is unestablished, and no open question excuses a shown
      violation. A shape that depends on S-01's evidence — S-02, S-03, S-04 — becomes UNRESOLVED
      only once that evidence is established; until then the Record is PENDING_EXTERNAL on it.
      Shapes that do not depend on it — D-04, D-05, E-04, E-08 — are UNRESOLVED at once.

DECISION MATRIX — a contract-level statement of X-01, not an algorithm and not a validator

  Case                                                                        Outcome
  a NATIVE rule violated — e.g. R-03, O-01, O-04, E-03                        REJECT
  a named Kind checked and shown undeclared, or declared under another model
  (E-07)                                                                      REJECT
  a named Kind checked, and its declared status cannot be established (E-07;
  RB-6)                                                                       REJECT
  a two-role World type, its scope established, lacking direction or an
  eligibility entry on a role (S-04)                                          REJECT
  an EXTERNAL check that establishes any other violation — E-09, M-01 to M-05,
  S-03's contradicted count                                                   REJECT
  any shown violation together with an open shape or a pending check          REJECT
  a source-gap shape (S-02, S-03, S-04, D-04, D-05, E-04), no violation       UNRESOLVED
  participants of different models, every named Kind's status established,
  permission undecided (E-08), no violation                                   UNRESOLVED
  a source-gap shape — E-08 included — together with a pending check other
  than the S-01 evidence the shape depends on, no violation                   UNRESOLVED
  a named Kind whose check has not run; or S-01's evidence, or a content
  limit, not yet established — and nothing above                              PENDING_EXTERNAL
  every NATIVE rule holds, every applicable EXTERNAL check is established by
  its owner, no shape is open                                                 CONFORMS

  An unrun check is never reported as failed. A checked-but-unestablished declared status is
  never PENDING_EXTERNAL or UNRESOLVED. A source gap is never reported as a failed lookup. A
  carrier's presence never establishes the legality of what it holds. E-08 never bypasses
  E-07, and E-07 is no ban on cross-model types.

The rules fix structure only. They derive no relationship type, role, owning role, direction,
eligible Kind or cardinality for any concrete type, and no rule of a model's relationship
architecture.

==================================================================================================
5. STRUCTURAL PROHIBITIONS, REJECTION REGISTER, PROHIBITED INFERENCES
==================================================================================================

P-01A This revision introduces no element or part beyond the eleven elements and seven parts of
      §1. A Record carrying any of the following does not conform to this revision (NATIVE):
      — instance or edge structure (079 RT-079-16; §6 SOVEREIGNTY): endpoint, endpoints,
        participant, participants, participant_id, source_record, target_record, edge, edges,
        edge_id, relationship_record, back_reference, graph, history, valid_from, valid_until,
        edge_provenance;
      — ownership application or a second owner carrier (079 §8.5; §4 O-03): is_owner, owner,
        owner_flag, owning_endpoint, owning_record, owning_model, holder, storage_location;
      — relationship-type cardinality (OD-079-1; §3 NOT REPRESENTED): cardinality, multiplicity,
        min, max, min_count, max_count, one_to_one, one_to_many, many_to_many, bounds;
      — invented direction semantics (SC-079-F): inverse, inverse_type, reverse_name,
        symmetric, transitive, reflexive, default_direction;
      — a model-scope or applicability element (§4 S-01): model, using_model, scope_model,
        applies_to_model;
      — a name or code element (§3 definition): name, type_name, label, code, type_code;
      — universal semantics or Registry status (RMS §4): status, tier, lifecycle_state,
        canonical, owner_model, kind_code, layer;
      — execution or runtime structure (RMS §10.2; RT-079-22): validator, resolver, engine,
        index, cache, session, process, service, worker, handler, implementation, verdict.
      The list explains P-01A; it does not exhaust it. P-01A binds this revision only: a later
      governed revision of this contract may add an element a governing source establishes.
P-01B This revision introduces no version, revision, latest-version, supersession, replacement,
      deprecation, retirement, effective-date, migration, compatibility or retention element or
      mechanism, and no rule that re-owns, rewrites or revalidates an edge when a definition
      changes. That representation is deferred to rows 108–110: neither defined nor
      permanently prohibited here (079 VS-079-1 to VS-079-3; RMS §10.2 lists "version ·
      supersession" among what the Registry may define). Whatever those rows establish stays
      Registry-owned, is not an envelope field (P-05) and is not a universal semantic (P-06).
P-02  No generic reference or dependency list, and no reference element 079 does not require:
      references, refs, dependencies, related_types, kind_definition_ref, model_definition_ref,
      relationship_type_ref, inverse_ref, field_definition_ref, schema_ref, extends, includes. The
      one concrete reference relation this family carries is eligibility (079 RF-079-1); an
      admissible target category alone authorizes nothing (RF-079-5; Artifact 063 RB-5).
P-03  No element names, carries or implies ownership of a relationship instance, an edge, a
      Relationship Record, a participant Record or a model's mechanism. The Registry owns this
      Record and the definition; each model owns its relationships (079 RT-079-10; RMS §15:
      "Relationship definitions; never runtime relationship ownership"; Artifact 061 §7 row 3).
P-04  Not a World Relationship Record schema, a relationship-instance schema or a type catalog.
      No element carries what an actual relationship holds, and no Relationship Record is
      required of any model (079 RT-079-11; I-102).
P-05  No envelope field added, removed or renamed. The family elements and parts are not envelope
      fields; role, owning_role, direction, version, status, tier and relationship_type never
      become one (RMS §4).
P-06  None of RMS §4's nine prohibited universal semantics: no Universal Record Base, Universal
      Relationship Record, Universal History Record, universal lifecycle, universal
      canonicality, universal Kind taxonomy, universal identity composition, universal state
      model or universal semantic schema. For this family: no universal role vocabulary, arity,
      direction grammar or relationship roster either (079 RT-079-23).
P-07  Not another family's contract: not KIND-, MODEL-, SUBTYPE-, FIELD- or SCHEMA-DEFINITION,
      CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY, CONSTRAINT-DEFINITION or VALIDATION-RULE. No element embeds another
      family's definitions.
P-08  No element records a lockstep pairing or partner. 079 ↔ 080 is no lockstep pair (SC-080-E),
      and LS-3's pairing of a model's relationships with their type definitions is not a
      reference (079 SC-079-P; 064 §13 Q7).
P-09  No dependency element. Eligibility is a declaration reference, not by itself a semantic
      dependency (Artifact 062 D-9). The family sits in L1 stratum 1b (062 §6); D-8 forbids its
      meaning to depend on L2–L5; concrete dependency rules are row 111's.
P-10  No element represents how a definition is proposed, approved, admitted or deprecated;
      governance is Artifact 065's.
P-11  No inbound reference: nothing here represents how an actual relationship or a Relationship
      Record identifies its type (079 SC-079-P), and no type-reference format is defined.

