8. SOURCE CONDITIONS
==================================================================================================

Each entry: the source statements, the condition, whether 080 owns its resolution, its treatment,
the remaining owner where one is established, and its effect.

SC-080-A  Registry classification and roster. Blueprint §9.4 classifies the Registry as a
          capability; RMS §10 closes that (COLLISION-1) — the Registry is a sovereign Record
          Model. RMS §10.1 fixes fourteen Registry Kinds, RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION Kind 6;
          Blueprint §13.6's RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEF is an alias (064 §5; 079 SC-079-A, SC-079-B).
          080 owns nothing here; no roster is revived and no Kind is created. CLOSED BY SOURCE;
          no effect on 080's completion.
SC-080-B  Registry references to Kinds. Blueprint §9.4 and §13.6e say a Registry definition "may
          never reference a kind, a subtype, or an instance"; RMS §10.3 corrects it — "v0.1
          stated the boundary too bluntly" — admitting declared Kinds and keeping domain
          instances forbidden (079 SC-079-R). role.eligibility.kind follows RMS §10.3. CLOSED BY
          SOURCE; no effect.
SC-080-C  Schema definition against execution. RMS §10.2: "SCHEMA-DEFINITION is a Registry
          Record." and "Registry does not execute schemas." Older wording that the Registry is
          not schema does not forbid this structural contract, which defines structure and
          executes nothing (§6 EXECUTION). CLOSED BY SOURCE; no effect.
SC-080-D  Open decisions inherited from 079 §19.1. OD-079-1 (what cardinality bounds; owner the
          Blueprint/RMS author, no row assigned) and OD-079-2 (what the owning role governs
          outside Relationship Records; owners rows 276, 338, 356, 366, escalating to the author).
          080 owns neither. Treatment: cardinality is not represented (§3); owning_role is
          represented as a declaration and its application is not (§6 DECLARATION AND
          APPLICATION; S-05). Neither is a G gate on 080 (row 080 carries G: —). Effect: 080's
          Val and Done do not depend on them; the type sets, 112, 116 and the model mechanisms
          are limited as 079 §19.1 states.
SC-080-E  LS metadata. Row 080 carries LS: LS-1 and Why: LS-3; PART III defines LS-1 as Kind spec ↔
          KIND-DEFINITION and LS-3 as Relationship ↔ Relationship-Type-Definition. A structural
          contract is neither (079 SC-079-I; 077 SC-077-B). Both values preserved; no 079 ↔ 080
          pair, no LS-1 pair and no lockstep class invented. Owner: the Roadmap author. ROADMAP
          ISSUE, recorded; no effect on completion.
SC-080-F  LS-3 verification pointer. 079 §22 reports, for its Why: LS-3 partner, that "lockstep
          tests are row 123's". Row 123 carries LS: LS-1,4,5,6,7,8 and does not list LS-3; rows
          217 (World) and 293 (Epistemic) list LS-1,LS-2,LS-3. No P, V or I test row listing LS-3
          was found in the repository copy. 080 uses the Roadmap's assignments (§6 LS) and does
          not repeat the pointer; 079, row 123 and the test rows are not edited, and no
          dependency or gate is created. Owner: 079's author for the pointer; the Roadmap author
          for LS-3 test coverage of P, V and I. UPSTREAM TRACEABILITY DISCREPANCY, recorded;
          non-blocking for 080.
SC-080-G  Manifest metadata against file status. Row 080 carries T: schema · Canon:
          canonical-about-meaning · CD: yes on a docs/** path; Artifact 003 gives a docs/**
          specification Canon: n/a and says CD "licenses nothing"; the Revolving Resolution
          Note records the same inconsistency for the rows AD-REG-AUTHORING-SPLIT moved under
          docs/registry/ (CONFLICT-F), of which 080 is one. The values are copied exactly; the
          effective status is §0 STATUS — an authored structural contract, not a Record,
          licensing no canonical write. Owner: the Roadmap author. Recorded, not resolved; no
          effect on completion.
SC-080-H  Req: RR-16 is carried exactly. Its text is not in the repository (Revolving Resolution
          Note, GAP-C); no text is stated and no requirement-level compliance is claimed.
          NON-BLOCKING, UNVERIFIED.
SC-080-I  Registry Kind code. No two-character Registry Kind code is established, and kind codes
          outside World are not frozen (Artifact 063 §9). The envelope kind is constrained
          symbolically; eligibility names Kinds, not codes. Owner: row 117. Non-blocking.
SC-080-J  Unlocks against consumers. Row 080's → (177, 277, 338, 352, 375) and the rows listing
          080 in H (198, 277, 338, 356, 366) differ: 177, 352 and 375 do not list 080 in H, and
          198, 356 and 366 are not in 080's → (079 SC-079-O). Both lists preserved; neither
          rewritten; an unlock is not a hard dependency. Owner: the Roadmap author. ROADMAP
          ISSUE, recorded; non-blocking.
SC-080-K  Realization and notation. The Blueprint names JSON Schema (ADOPT) and LinkML (ADAPT) as
          realizations (§12.15, §26.3b). This file follows the repository's local
          structural-contract notation (§0) and adopts no serialization, schema language or
          generated validator; no parser exists for the notation. Recorded.
SC-080-L  Declared status has no single proof mechanism across the six models (Artifact 063
          SC-063-H). role.eligibility.kind's declared status is therefore EXTERNAL; for
          role.eligibility.model the closed set is the declared set. Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-080-M  WSV as a participant. RMS §7 places WSV as "always the non-owning endpoint" of World's
          pressure edges, while row 231 says "WSV is World state, not a Kind" and Blueprint §13.10
          is headed PROPOSED (079 SC-079-M). (W, WSV) is rejected as an eligible Kind (E-03),
          because WSV is not a Kind. How a World pressure-edge type states WSV's end is World's
          (rows 197–198); 080 neither represents nor forbids another form. SOURCE GAP for World;
          non-blocking for 080.
SC-080-N  Remaining representation and semantic gaps, each bounded:
            — non-World arity (079 SC-079-E): UNRESOLVED until the model's architecture states it
              (S-03); owner the model rows;
            — Model-only eligibility and participants of several models (079 SC-079-G; Artifact
              058 §8.4): UNRESOLVED (E-04, E-08); owners the model rows and 058's successors; no
              matrix invented;
            — combination rules among eligibility entries: none represented; a list names Kinds
              that may each stand, nothing more;
            — a World type whose endpoints stand in the same role (079 SC-079-Q): UNRESOLVED
              (S-02, D-04); owner World (197–198);
            — World types of three or more roles: UNRESOLVED (S-02; SC-080-T);
            — a legality constraint admitting every Kind at an end, or no Kind: not
              representable; no source establishes either, and a World type needing one is
              outside this revision (S-04);
            — direction vocabulary, inverse types, symmetry, transitivity (079 SC-079-F): not
              represented; no owner established;
            — direction for types of more than two roles: UNRESOLVED (D-05);
            — §13.3 scope for E, P, V, I (079 SC-079-H): UNRESOLVED (S-04); owners the model rows.
          None blocks 080's Val or Done: each is a shape a Record may have, held open.
SC-080-O  Inbound type references (079 SC-079-P; 064 §13 Q7). How an actual relationship or a
          Relationship Record identifies its type is not established; 080 defines nothing for it
          (P-11). Owner: each model's relationship-record and type rows (e.g. 199). Non-blocking.
SC-080-P  Reification wording residual (079 SC-079-S). RMS §15's criterion and §13.9's custody use
          two senses of "own", reconciled in 079 §10 and not stated in the sources' own text.
          080 represents the custody side only — owning_role — and decides no reification.
          Owner: the Blueprint/RMS author. Non-blocking.
SC-080-Q  Row 366's Val is printed in the repository copy as **SECTION, with no closing emphasis
          and no further text. 080 does not interpret it, cites it as printed, and adds nothing to
          it (§6 DOWNSTREAM). Owner: the Roadmap author. Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-080-R  registry_ref referent. Artifact 033 leaves the referent unresolved; 080 attaches none
          and uses registry_ref for neither eligibility nor the owning role (§2). Non-blocking.
SC-080-S  Version representation and Registry evolution (079 VS-079-1 to VS-079-3). Deferred to
          rows 108–110; not defined and not permanently prohibited (P-01B). Non-blocking.
SC-080-T  Declared roles against World endpoints. Blueprint §13.9: "An edge joins two objects.";
          079 §7 defines a participant role as "a position that a participant occupies in every
          relationship of the type" and synthesizes "two participant positions, one at each end"
          for World; 079 §8.4 and SC-079-Q nonetheless leave open two endpoints standing in the
          same role. Condition: no source maps declared roles onto endpoints one-to-one — neither
          that each endpoint occupies its own role, nor that an endpoint occupies at most one.
          Treatment: the two-role shape the sources show is admissible; one role, and three or
          more, are UNRESOLVED (S-02), not rejected and not accepted. 080 does not own the
          question and edits nothing upstream; 079's role definition and its same-role gap are
          recorded together here as an upstream observation. Owner: World's relationship
          architecture and type set (rows 197–198), with the Blueprint/RMS author where the
          answer needs source text. Non-blocking for 080's Val and Done.
SC-080-U  Placement. Row 080 of the repaired Roadmap names docs/registry/relationship_type.schema.
          Roadmap §0.8 records why: "Twenty-two P3 rows targeted canon/registry/**", which only
          the Mutation Coordinator may write, and its ruling, marked AUTHOR-DECIDED
          (AD-REG-AUTHORING-SPLIT), says "Structural contracts — rows 067, 069, 071, 073, 077, 080,
          082, 084, 087, 089, 091, 093, 095, 097, 099, 102, 104 — move to
          docs/registry/<family>.schema" while "Canon, CD, SoT, H, S and LS of the moved rows are
          preserved". A copy of the Roadmap that predates §0.8 shows row 080 under
          canon/registry/; that copy is superseded by §0.8 and by the row as it now stands. The
          literal row path, the path §0.8 assigns and this file's location agree. canon/registry/
          remains the zone of committed Registry Records, written only through row 152 after
          G-CANON-R; this file is not such a Record and is not copied there. Recorded; CLOSED BY
          SOURCE; no effect on 080's completion.

